NOTES / DEVIATIONS
- zero-shot model = work/pretrained (GENCO Base, hidden 48, 20.1 M parameters), no fine-tuning. Its pretraining task ("PreTraining", random feature masking, mask_p 0.1-0.8) does not exist in the installed graphkit 0.9.0.3; it is run here with the PowerFlow mask (the same mask the released per-grid checkpoints use). So it is zero-shot in grid AND evaluated on one specific mask pattern.
- normaliser: no normalizer_stats.pt ships with the pretrained model. HeteroDataMVANormalizer is fitted per network by graphkit (baseMVA = p95 of non-zero Pd, Qd, gen p_mw, bus Qg; vn_kv_max); the same recipe was applied to the scenarios of each unseen grid (118: 141.41, 500: 146.40, 1354: 333.33, 2000: 124.57). The recipe uses the solved Qg (one scalar per grid). Sensitivity on 8 base states of IEEE 118 (baseMVA 57 / 100 / 114.6 / 137.9 / 230): raw error median 4.06 / 4.14 / 4.17 / 4.46 / 4.94 points, zs+1 missed 8/60 in every case - the choice does not matter (work/zeroshot/logs/report_smoke_and_basemva_sensitivity.log).
- per-grid reference "pg": IEEE 118 = released Base, GOC 500 and GOC 2000 = released Tiny (model size differs from the zero-shot Base). PEGASE 1354: no released checkpoint exists in gridfm/genco-pf-datakit, none downloaded.
- scenario counts: IEEE 118 2,996 (600 load scenarios x 5 topology variants, 4 dropped by datakit); GOC 500 2,998 = the first 600 of 3,000 load scenarios of the existing set (14,992); PEGASE 1354 1,339 (300 load scenarios requested, 32 with infeasible OPF, 1 PF failure -> 268 base states); GOC 2000 all 2,494.
- IEEE 118 and PEGASE 1354 are heavily loaded under this perturbation family (83.9% / 57.3% of scenarios have a real overload), so "secure flagged" rests on 481 / 572 secure scenarios.
- zs = the model's own branch flows; zs0 = its voltages through the exact branch equations; zs1/zs2 = after 1/2 Newton steps. hybzs = pre-outage AC voltages + zero-shot delta. anch_zs = pre-outage AC loading + zero-shot loading delta (no Newton).
- GOC 2000 pg/prev/hybpg rows reproduce work/prev_control.log and work/hybrid_control.log exactly (1 / 2 / 0 missed of 369).
